                    {
                        "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                        "entry_id": "e0be0aa4-5975-3359-b5b9-899eea57a4cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of boogie.",
                            "To dance to boogie music; to get down."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "df3da609-eae7-49a4-8b41-f961274a82f2",
                                "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                                "text": "How was he supposed to boogy with one acoustic ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1aeb1f23-b8c2-4067-b866-98db1492c42b",
                                "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                                "text": "He could hear the hi-fi going next door, Lesley boogying around the apartment to the Bee-Gees, ignoring her aunt, who was a little deaf."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7a61860-1c6e-4658-ac7a-4e0e7d2ea541",
                                "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                                "text": "South Africans of any skin color were all out there on the floor and had decisions to make: not whether to boogy, but whom to boogy with."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "089b1e70-d1de-40f6-837d-f2cb0239c06f",
                                "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                                "text": "\"There will be a big band, so you will have to dance with me.\" \"And I shall.\" \"No boogying, don't worry.\" “Do you think me incapable of boogying?”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50e7400c-476e-4f20-8f80-a7e045006efc",
                                "sense_id": "066ca02a-80db-3f76-ac3e-b281313febad",
                                "text": "Are they boogying and do they know how?' asks Johnny."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6c3dff4-0a97-3d47-82b2-5ba1e0625953",
                        "entry_id": "e0be0aa4-5975-3359-b5b9-899eea57a4cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of boogie.",
                            "To move, travel, or exit; to sashay."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9935784-732e-4539-8e89-34c8006bbf26",
                                "sense_id": "b6c3dff4-0a97-3d47-82b2-5ba1e0625953",
                                "text": "Well I'm boogying around there and this panther ain't crossed my mind that it'd be this panther that come back."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8e5e269-dd5e-42a5-866d-e7603269fbba",
                                "sense_id": "b6c3dff4-0a97-3d47-82b2-5ba1e0625953",
                                "text": "And talking of dopes, why don't you boogy on over to Thresher for a refresher."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "775d7663-67d0-4c96-b822-de3a46f5fb0f",
                                "sense_id": "b6c3dff4-0a97-3d47-82b2-5ba1e0625953",
                                "text": "There I was in the middle of the night boogying down the avenue and suddenly there was a cow and he boogied right over and there was yellow cake everywhere."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7777216e-e338-33c5-afc7-3aa37e2c4dcb",
                        "entry_id": "e0be0aa4-5975-3359-b5b9-899eea57a4cb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To have sex."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aeff77fd-9882-41e2-84a2-12a9816bfa52",
                                "sense_id": "7777216e-e338-33c5-afc7-3aa37e2c4dcb",
                                "text": "This book was originally written in the \"boogy down\" year of 1974 – right in the middle of the 1970's when the dating scene finally broke free from the restrictions of the \"Ozzie & Harriet\" 1950's and the unwashed \"Love Bead\" 1960's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a9a9175e-7be7-42d0-bd41-d6259ff5b978",
                                "sense_id": "7777216e-e338-33c5-afc7-3aa37e2c4dcb",
                                "text": "Boogying with him would be fun."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7e78b041-4edd-3aa1-9118-9e83db6b6521",
                        "entry_id": "e0be0aa4-5975-3359-b5b9-899eea57a4cb",
